course: dictionary
lesson: 13237
title: Genetic: words about genes
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from science, and small clues inside them help you work out what they mean. Genetic has gene inside it, and genes are tiny instructions inside living cells. «Her blue eyes are a genetic gift from her mum.» Blue eyes come from instructions passed from parents, so genetic must mean to do with genes.
explain: Genetic is an adjective, and genetically is its adverb. «The seeds were genetically modified to grow faster.» The word modified tells you the seeds were changed, and genetically tells you how: by changing their genes. Look at the words around a hard word before you reach for a dictionary.
explain: Try the swap check. Put a simple idea in place of genetic: «Her blue eyes are a gene gift from her mum.» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: Genetic means to do with genes.
fact: Genes are tiny instructions inside living cells, passed from parents to children.
fact: Genes help decide things like eye colour.
fact: «Genetic engineering» means changing genes on purpose.
fact: A «genetic disease» is an illness passed down through genes.
exercise: «Her blue eyes are a genetic gift from her mum.» What does genetic mean here? | To do with food | To do with the sea | To do with music | *To do with genes
exercise: «The doctor said the illness is genetic, so it runs in the family.» Why is the illness called genetic? | It only happens in hospitals | It is caught from a dog | *It is passed down in families through genes | It goes away after one day
exercise: «Scientists use genetic engineering to change genes.» What does genetic engineering mean? | Building bridges with steel | Cooking with fresh genes | Painting pictures in a studio | *Changing genes on purpose
test: «Ruby has her dad's curly hair because it is a genetic feature.» What does genetic feature mean? | A feature that is painted on | *A feature passed down from parents through genes | A feature that happens once at school | A feature of the weather
test: «The seeds were genetically modified to grow faster.» What does genetically modified mean? | *Changed by altering their genes | Painted bright colours | Sold in a shop | Grown without any water
exam: «Each child gets a mix of genetic information from both parents.» Where does this genetic information come from? | The sun | The shop | The school | *Both parents
